'''''Diospyros ferrea''''', known as '''black ebony''', is a tree in the [[Ebenaceae|ebony family]], distributed in  Burma (Myanmar), Cambodia, India, Indonesia, Malay Peninsula, Philippines, Sri Lanka, Thailand, Laos ([[Khammouane province|Khammouan]]) and Taiwan ([[Hengchun Peninsula]] and [[Orchid Island]]).

==Distribution==
It is found from West Africa to India, Indo-China, north to the [[Ryukyu Island]]s (Japan), east to the Malesian area, Australia, [[Melanesia]] and [[Polynesia]].

==Uses==
''D. ferrea'' is reported to be an important source of black ebony, but this is doubtful because of the unsatisfactory taxonomy of the group involved.{{Citation needed|date=May 2024}}

